Z||000008||stsmithgt||05-18-2001||11:46 AM||||Things that make you go. ?????????<BR>When stopping a check, how many of you think that's it, the check is void, over, and done with? Note: The Federal Government limits the banks from stopping payment on a check to SIX months.  At that time, you'd have to  renew the stop, with additional service charges, on that check because it is now valid again and can be processed.  If it's a big check, I would keep this in mind.  I found this out through Bank of America.  It all sounds stupid.  I don't know how the FED's came up with this or maybe the B of A employee is wrong, but I would ask at the bank you do business with if your planning on stopping a significant check.  I stopped a $500.00 one and found this out with a lucky question I asked, "So I never have to worry about this check ever again?  Especially if someone tries to process it?"  <BR>As many checks as I've written for my Fiero, I feel lucky I haven't had to stop any. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>My heap. No, it's not missing the "C".<BR>Those are notes that I spend on it.<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
